  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p21-q13-definition-paragraph",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Pairs of rational numbers are called ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "perfect partners",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " if their sum is equal to their product. For example, ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "3",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac32",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " are perfect partners since ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "3+\\frac32=\\frac92",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "3\\times\\frac32=\\frac92",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q13-a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find a perfect partner for each of these rational numbers:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p21-q13-a-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$\\frac53$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac52$",
              "worked": "Let the partner be $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac53+x&=\\frac53x\\\\\\frac53&=\\frac23x\\\\x&=\\frac53\\div\\frac23\\\\x&=\\frac52\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac53+\\frac52=\\frac{25}{6}$ and $\\frac53\\times\\frac52=\\frac{25}{6}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 66
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q13-a-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$\\frac35$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-\\frac32$",
              "worked": "Let the partner be $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac35+x&=\\frac35x\\\\\\frac35&=-\\frac25x\\\\x&=\\frac35\\div\\left(-\\frac25\\right)\\\\x&=-\\frac32\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac35-\\frac32=-\\frac9{10}$ and $\\frac35\\times\\left(-\\frac32\\right)=-\\frac9{10}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 66
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q13-a-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\frac97$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac92$",
              "worked": "Let the partner be $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac97+x&=\\frac97x\\\\\\frac97&=\\frac27x\\\\x&=\\frac97\\div\\frac27\\\\x&=\\frac92\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac97+\\frac92=\\frac{81}{14}$ and $\\frac97\\times\\frac92=\\frac{81}{14}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 66
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q13-a-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$\\frac2{13}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-\\frac2{11}$",
              "worked": "Let the partner be $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac2{13}+x&=\\frac2{13}x\\\\\\frac2{13}&=-\\frac{11}{13}x\\\\x&=\\frac2{13}\\div\\left(-\\frac{11}{13}\\right)\\\\x&=-\\frac2{11}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac2{13}-\\frac2{11}=-\\frac4{143}$ and $\\frac2{13}\\times\\left(-\\frac2{11}\\right)=-\\frac4{143}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 66
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Do all rational numbers have a perfect partner? When a rational number has a perfect partner, is it unique?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No. $1$ has no perfect partner. Every other rational number $r$ has the unique perfect partner $\\frac{r}{r-1}$.\n\nSet $r+x=rx$ and solve for $x$.",
          "worked": "For a rational number $r$, let its partner be $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}r+x&=rx\\\\r&=(r-1)x\\\\x&=\\frac{r}{r-1}\\qquad(r\\ne1)\\end{align*}$$\nIf $r=1$, the defining equation is $1+x=x$, which is impossible. If $r\\ne1$, division by the nonzero number $r-1$ gives exactly one rational value of $x$. It is a partner because\n$$\\begin{align*}r+\\frac{r}{r-1}&=\\frac{r(r-1)+r}{r-1}\\\\r+\\frac{r}{r-1}&=\\frac{r^2}{r-1}\\\\r\\times\\frac{r}{r-1}&=\\frac{r^2}{r-1}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 88
      }
    ]
  },
